diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket's premise is incorrect — the internal web portal web1.local
is fully operational at the time of investigation. Every layer of the stack was
verified:

DNS: The authoritative server (dns_server, 10.200.0.2) holds a correct A record
"web1 IN A 10.200.0.4" in the "local" zone, and nslookup from host_1_1_1_1
resolves web1.local to 10.200.0.4 without error.

Network path: OSPF has converged correctly on all three core routers. The
traceroute from host_1_1_1_1 shows a clean five-hop path (switch_dist_1_1 →
router_core_1 → router_core_3 → switch_server_access → web_server_1) with
sub-millisecond latency per hop and zero packet loss. The reachability matrix
confirms all hosts reach all other hosts at 0% loss.

Web service: Apache/2.4.62 on web_server_1 has been running without errors since
lab start (03:17 UTC). It listens on 0.0.0.0:80, iptables is fully open, and a
live HTTP GET from host_1_1_1_1 returned "HTTP/1.1 200 OK" with the correct
page content ("Welcome to Web Server 1"). The Apache access log confirms the
request was served successfully.

Root cause: There is no fault; the reported outage does not correspond to any
actual network or service failure present in the lab.

Corrective action: No remediation is needed. The operations team should follow
up directly with the users to confirm whether they may have been hitting a
browser-side cache issue, a temporary transient blip, or a mistaken report.
Web_server_1 does not need to be rebooted.
=== END ===
